WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.150
Speaker 1: We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.900
That number is 2192.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:13.259
David P, here is a caller who is worried about
me, and I always appreciate concern from people

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:14.259
in the audience.

00:00:14.259 --> 00:00:15.640
Speaker 4: Hey, David, it's James.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.770
I was watching some of your earlier videos
from earlier, but this is from a couple of

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.770
years ago.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.770
One in particular stands out.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:22.920
I believe it was called CALLER Needs help
with Jewish Person.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.490
And you seem like you're in a much better
place.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.850
You are in much higher spirits of the times.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:32.279
Really joyful the venue you have recently.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:34.480
How are you?

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.950
All right.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.160
There's something happened.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.250
You seem kind of down in the dumps recently.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.250
Well.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.629
Speaker 1: The concern, nothing in particular
has happened.

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:53.540
Certainly the state of affairs in the United
States is quite sad.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.540
That is true.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:00.670
So I think it would be logical as someone
who is steeped in how things are going to

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.329
be sort of concerned.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:07.680
But at the same time, the video that the caller
is referring to, I believe happened while

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.250
Trump was president, which was certainly a
dark time in American history.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.350
So, no, I appreciate the concern.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.350
Nothing in particular is wrong.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:18.050
I mean, listen, let's be honest.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.930
Chasing around a baby is exhausting.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:29.610
So if anything could be blamed for tiredness
or whatever, certainly it would be it would

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.610
be that.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.610
But no, everything is fine.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.610
Thanks for asking.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.450
On the bonus show today, folks.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.820
We have a fantastic bonus show today.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.420
I just got back from a wedding in California.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.850
I am going to talk about elements that took
place on the flight, some unfortunate confrontations

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.850
that took place.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.850
Not good.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:53.200
I'm going to talk about running into some
really nice folks who watched the show while

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.170
I was in the Bay Area of California, met some
great people just by chance.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.049
There was no event or anything.

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:01.560
Just ran into some great people.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.340
I am going to talk about what else am I going
to talk about?

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.340
I have stories.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.000
I have stories from California.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:16.130
We are also going to talk about an investigation
into the cause of the implosion of that Titanic

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:17.209
submersible.

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:19.250
We're going to discuss that.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:23.320
And also, Japan has a plan to boost birth
rates.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.610
We've talked about the plan before.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.540
Is it a viable plan?

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.330
We're starting to gather data.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:37.760
One city has reason to hope that this is a
good plan for Japan to raise birth rates,

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.710
where birth rates are getting dangerously
low.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:46.370
From a political standpoint, all of those
stories and more will be in none other than

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.959
today's bonus show.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.140
Speaker 2: Oh, the bonus show where you want
to make money.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.140
Yeah.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.430
Speaker 3: Everybody else that makes money
to fund themselves is bad.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:57.790
Speaker 1: And of course, after being back
for one day, I will be off for the next three

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.790
weeks.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.790
No, I'm kidding.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:00.790
We're back.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.720
We're back for a while before before the next
break.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.709
It's not even really a break anymore, you
know.

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:07.810
By the way, let's just talk a little bit about
the guest hosts.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.129
Every time we have guest hosts, I get e-mails.

00:03:10.129 --> 00:03:11.150
All right.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.800
I'm going to tell everybody right now.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.480
I know that not everybody likes the guest
hosts.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.540
I know it because every guest host we have
no matter what.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.210
We get e-mails from people saying I couldn't
bear to watch it.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.319
Some people liked Luke, but they didn't like
Pat.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:31.049
Some people like Pat, but they didn't like
Luke.

00:03:31.049 --> 00:03:32.720
Some people didn't like either.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.200
Some people said both were fine, but it wasn't
that good.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.650
So I'm just going to put it out there.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.730
We used to have no shows when I would be away.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.130
It wasn't really.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.950
Robust.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.830
One of the things I've wanted to do is have
a more robust show that can continue when

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.870
I'm gone.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.360
We now have multiple people who can do the
producer role.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.340
We have a rotating cast of guest hosts.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:02.900
I understand and I'm flattered that when I'm
gone.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.739
Some people say, David, I'd rather have you
here.

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:08.209
And that makes sense because you're watching
this show or listening to this show rather

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:09.209
than some other show.

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:12.130
So I get that and I love that and I'm flattered
by it.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.220
But you don't have to email me that you don't
like the guest hosts or all of the guest hosts,

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.160
because I know that not everybody likes them.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.810
Viewership goes down when we have a guest
host.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:28.010
But my opinion is and people in the audience
seem to agree it's better to have a guest

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:35.139
host rather than no show or a repeat show,
because if it's part of your routine to listen

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:38.389
to a podcast on the way to work, on the way
to the gym, whatever, and you don't necessarily

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:42.479
want to find something else, we have something
there, and I think viewership is usually down

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:46.320
about 30% when we have guest host, which isn't
really that bad, I have to tell you.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.320
All right.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.870
So you you can always email for any reason,
but if you're just emailing in to say, hey,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:57.050
I didn't like the guest hosts, we know we
see that in the data and we're going to continue

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:03.020
working to have a great rotating slate of
hosts that will hold down the fort until I

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.020
get back.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.880
I'll write more about my trip on the bonus
show.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.410
We'll be back tomorrow.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.570
We have a very strong week of programing.

